= Introduction {#sec:intro}

== Purpose

This document specifies the design of the integration between the ACME
checkout service and the \gateway{} payment gateway.\footnote{\gateway{} API
version 2024-11 is assumed throughout; see \link[https://docs.payflow.example/v2024-11]{the
vendor documentation}.} It is intended for developers, testers and the
security review board.

== Scope

The integration covers card authorisation, capture, refunds (@sec:refunds)
and asynchronous notifications (@sec:webhooks). Recurring billing is _out of
scope_ and will be addressed in a separate specification.

== Definitions

\table[style="Acme Grid", header-rows=1, widths=(4cm, 1fr), id=tbl:defs]{
  | Term          | Definition                                                     |
  | Authorisation | A hold placed on the cardholder's funds.                        |
  | Capture       | Settlement of a previously authorised amount.                    |
  | Idempotency key | A client-generated UUID that makes a request safe to retry.    |
}
\caption[@tbl:defs, above]{Definitions}

= Architecture {#sec:arch}

\figure[id=fig:context, width=15cm, align=center]{
  \image{img/context-diagram.png}
  \caption{System context}
}

As shown in @fig:context, the checkout service never handles raw card
numbers: card data is tokenised in the browser by the \gateway{} SDK.

== Components

- *Checkout API*: receives orders from the web shop.
- *Payment Adapter*: translates domain commands into \gateway{} API calls.
  It is the only component holding gateway credentials.
- *Webhook Receiver*: verifies and persists gateway events (@sec:webhooks).

= Functional Requirements {#sec:reqs}

== Authorisation

\req[id=req:auth-amount]{The adapter shall send amounts in minor currency units.}
\req[id=req:auth-idem]{Every authorisation request shall carry an idempotency key.}
\req[id=req:auth-timeout, priority=Should]{The adapter should time out after 10~s
and retry at most twice, reusing the idempotency key (see \ref{req:auth-idem}).}

== Refunds {#sec:refunds}

\req[id=req:refund-partial]{Partial refunds shall be supported up to the captured amount.}

\note[kind=warning]{Refunds older than 180 days are rejected by \gateway{} and must
be handled manually by Finance.}

== Webhooks {#sec:webhooks}

Events are signed with HMAC-SHA256. The receiver verifies the signature
before parsing the body:

```python {#lst:verify, caption="Webhook signature verification"}
def verify(payload: bytes, header: str, secret: bytes) -> bool:
    expected = hmac.new(secret, payload, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()
    return hmac.compare_digest(expected, header)
```

Listing \ref[form=number]{lst:verify} uses a constant-time comparison.

